1	/*
2	 * CHAOSCov — single-run hardware coverage instrumentation for the
3	 * Harpocrates reproduction (harp plan Task 1.2; metrics per ISCA'24 §II-D).
4	 *
5	 * Two coverage families (definitions mirror the paper exactly):
6	 *   ACE lifetime (bit arrays: IRF, L1D, LSQ): ACE cycles / total ROI cycles
7	 *     summed over all bits, i.e. AVF. Upper bound of transient-fault
8	 *     detection capability.
9	 *   IBR (functional units): effective input bits delivered to the unit /
10	 *     theoretical max (full-width inputs at every ROI cycle). Correlates
11	 *     with (does not bound) permanent gate-level fault detection.
12	 *
13	 * ROI gating: m5ops workbegin/workend markers (inserted by tools/harp_wrap.py)
14	 * flip roi_active. Collection hooks short-circuit when !roi_active.
15	 * The pseudo_inst.cc side calls harp_cov_notify_work_begin/end() (weak
16	 * default no-op in CHAOSCov.cc; CHAOSCov registers itself there).
17	 *
18	 * This skeleton registers stats + detail dump; per-structure collectors
19	 * arrive in plan Tasks 2.x/3.x/4.1.
20	 */
